# What the next Firebase Test Lab run does. Edit and push to run again.
# (2026-10-22, fourth run: run 39741227453 was the first to change quality
# on a phone — 240p at 361 s and 366 s, back to Auto at 283 s and 294 s,
# never 00:00 — but Auto took 11 s on the realme, 8 of them waiting on the
# server for the copies it already held. A choice between copies now picks
# from the held grant; a check waits six seconds for the picture to move.)
# (2026-10-22, third run: the jump checks now drive the player screen's own
# controller. Run 39206916255 held one read before the screen had mounted,
# with nothing open in it: every change of quality was refused as "cannot be
# renewed" and the swipe seeked live as for a file — no quality change had
# been tried on a phone yet. A check now waits for the position to land
# near the target, not merely past it.)
# (2026-10-19, second run: the same checks, now waiting for the picture to
# MOVE after each jump and timing it — the first run passed a film stuck at
# the seek target for 45 s. The Worker now mends the chapter track's stray
# sidx that made every seek read the whole film; the app reopens at the
# right moment and does not take a seek's fill for a stall.)
# (2026-10-19: MODE=stream — Sintel through the real API on a realme C53 and
# an OPPO A38, with the jump checks of lib/app.dart: a seek, a change of
# quality, a +30 s skip, a swipe back, back to Auto, each checked for where
# it landed ("LAB check … PASS|FAIL"). 1.64.68 reopened at 00:00 after a
# quality change and after a slow seek.)
# (2026-10-15: MODE=crawl — this branch, the 1.64.64 candidate, crawled by
# Robo for ten minutes on a realme C53 and an OPPO A38: any crash, any
# "Something didn't load" card, on phones people in Myanmar carry. The
# Infinix and TECNO of 11 Oct sat in Test Lab's queue for 90 minutes.)
# (2026-10-11: Infinix and TECNO, which the 10 Oct run did not reach; the
# free test film through the real API on phones Myanmar
# carries — realme, OPPO, Infinix, TECNO, and the 32-bit build on an old
# Samsung — after the fix for the launch address that kept every game loop
# on "Route not found".)
#
# Physical phones, as "model,android-version". The free (Spark) plan allows
# five physical-device tests a day; each line here is one. The workflow
# writes the full list of models Test Lab has into the results, so this can
# be changed to what Myanmar actually carries.
DEVICES="RE58C2,35 OP5759L1,34"
# Phones that run 32-bit Android (MODE=playback or stream): they get the
# armeabi-v7a lab build, in a matrix of their own, since the arm64 APK does
# not install on them (the Galaxy A10 answered "Incompatible Architecture"
# in run 37967931084). They count against the same five a day.
DEVICES32=""
# Which release to test: "latest" or a tag such as v1.64.49-362.
APK_TAG=v1.64.49-362
# How long Robo may explore after the scripted part, in seconds.
TIMEOUT=600
# The phone's language for the run (my = Burmese).
LOCALE=my
# What the run does:
#   robo     — the released APK (APK_TAG), crawled by Robo after the script.
#   playback — this branch built as an arm64 lab APK; Test Lab's game loop
#              plays a pushed 720p film three ways (HW copy-back, HW direct,
#              software), ~50 s each, while CpuProbe logs every thread.
#              A25 (Exynos) and A34 (Dimensity, Android 16) draw with Vulkan;
#              A03s (MediaTek on Android 13) with OpenGL ES.
#              Two game-loop scenarios per phone: 1 = SurfaceTexture video
#              output, 2 = SurfaceProducer (1.64.54), same film, same script.
#   crawl    — this branch as an arm64 lab APK, crawled by Robo after
#              ROBO_SCRIPT (default robo/movies.json; start.json only steps
#              past the introduction and opens the Video tab's ⋮).
#   stream   — this branch as an arm64 lab APK; game-loop scenario 3 plays
#              STREAM_TITLE (a FREE catalogue title) the way a viewer's tap
#              does — request-playback, the Worker, R2, Auto's rung, the
#              proxy — on the phone's own connection, for four minutes.
MODE=stream
# MODE=robo / crawl: the Robo script that runs before the crawl.
ROBO_SCRIPT=test_device/robo/start.json
# Set to an earlier run's id to only collect its results again from Test
# Lab's bucket (BUCKET) — no test is run and no quota is spent. Empty = run.
FETCH_RUN=
BUCKET=test-lab-a83h77c3x52vk-yvsvq7a2052yz
# MODE=stream: the catalogue title to play (Sintel, the free test film).
STREAM_TITLE=0839dacb-59ae-4c95-9279-4901b925965d
